<%# locals: (tabs:, active:, aria_label:, title:, subtitle: nil, badge: nil, title_action: nil, right_content: nil, below_tab: false) %>
<%#
  The ONE area header: title box and tab bar, rendered by one file so they
  cannot disagree about the left edge.

  ⚠️ That is the whole point of this partial, and it is why the title box is in
  here rather than at the call site. Before this, the edge had TWO owners in the
  times area: NeoTitleBoxComponent sets its own margin (none, so it lands on the
  page edge from `main`), while the tab bar inherited an `mx-4 md:mx-5` from the
  div its caller wrapped it in. Title at 24px, tabs at 44px, on the same page.
  Management never had the problem because its subnav already rendered both.
  A caller that wraps this partial in a margin re-creates the split, which is
  what spec/views/one_page_edge_guard_spec.rb watches for.

  Tabs are siblings of the title, so nothing here is indented, and the bar holds
  tabs ONLY - tools belong one row lower.

  The active marker is edge-strong (border-ink), never an accent colour. The
  management bar used to mark active with border-cobalt-600, and cobalt-600 IS
  the accent (--accent in application.tailwind.css), so one token carried three
  meanings: main action, accent, active tab. Owning the marker here is what
  keeps a caller from picking a colour again.

  A bar with one tab is no bar: there is nothing to switch to. The title box
  then takes the wider gap, because it is the last thing before the content.

  @param tabs [Array<Hash>] {key:, label:, path:} from NavigationHelper, plus
    locked: true and locked_title: (the reason) on a tab that does not open
    yet: the AI tabs while AI is off (NavigationHelper#ai_section_tabs). A
    locked tab stays in the row, as the AI hub keeps its locked rows, and is
    no link but a span marked aria-disabled, as those rows are. It carries a
    lock sign, which the rows do not, and its label is faint (text-faint), the
    tone a locked row gives only its description (the row's name is
    text-muted). The reason is its tooltip and is read once more to screen
    readers. Opened by its URL anyway, it is the active tab like any other (the
    marker in place of the faint label, aria-current), still no link and still
    with the lock. A locked tab without a reason raises.
  @param active [Symbol] the tab that is current (with below_tab: the tab the
    page belongs to)
  @param aria_label [String] names the nav for screen readers
  ⚠️ The bar looks the SAME on every page, whatever comes below it. What
  follows adapts; never the other way round. So the rule and the gap are not
  negotiable per caller: the active tab's 2px underline sits on the bar's OWN
  rule via -mb-px, and that is the only line it may dock onto. An earlier build
  let a full-bleed filter stripe take the rule over and dropped the gap - the
  underline then ended on the top edge of a foreign element, with two lines of
  different owners (2px ink, short; 1px hairline, long) meeting in one row of
  pixels.

  On a phone the bar is ONE row (since 2026-11-11): below md the tabs keep
  their line and the row scrolls sideways, without a scrollbar (scrollbar-hide,
  as the ticket list's strip), and tab_strip_controller keeps the open tab in
  view by moving the row, never the page. Wrapped, the six KI tabs took two
  rows there, and an open tab of the first row had its underline in the middle
  of the bar instead of on its rule. From md on the row wraps as before.
  Measured in spec/system/management_phone_spec.rb.

  @param subtitle [String] the line under the title where it is not the
    organisation's name: the account area has no organisation and names the
    person (the preferences). Without it the title box names the organisation.
  @param title_action / right_content [String] captured blocks from the caller
  @param below_tab [Boolean] the page is not the active tab itself but a page
    below it (a form or a record of that tab, which names itself in the crumb
    line under the bar, organisations/shared/_section_crumb). The tab then reads
    as the parent: aria-current="true" ("you are in here") instead of "page"
    ("this is the page"), so a page has one aria-current="page", the crumb's.
    The tab looks the same either way: the marker says where the reader is.
%>
<% has_bar = tabs.size > 1 %>
<% active_tab_current = below_tab ? "true" : "page" %>
<%= render NeoTitleBoxComponent.new(
      title: title,
      subtitle: subtitle,
      badge: badge,
      variant: :organisation,
      margin_bottom: has_bar ? 'mb-3.5' : 'mb-6'
    ) do |box| %>
  <% box.with_title_action { title_action } if title_action.present? %>
  <% box.with_right_content { right_content } if right_content.present? %>
<% end %>

<% if has_bar %>
  <nav class="border-b border-cream-300 mb-3.5" aria-label="<%= aria_label %>">
    <%# One box and one active marker for every tab, link or locked, so a locked
        tab stands and marks exactly where an open one would. %>
    <% tab_box = 'inline-block border-b-2 pb-3 pt-1 text-sm whitespace-nowrap' %>
    <% active_marker = 'border-ink text-cream-900 font-bold' %>
    <ul class="flex overflow-x-auto scrollbar-hide gap-x-6 gap-y-1 md:flex-wrap md:overflow-visible md:gap-x-8 -mb-px"
        data-controller="tab-strip">
      <% tabs.each do |tab| %>
        <% is_active = (active.to_sym == tab[:key]) %>
        <li>
          <% if tab[:locked] %>
          <% reason = tab.fetch(:locked_title) %>
          <%= tag.span aria: { current: (is_active ? active_tab_current : nil), disabled: true }, title: reason,
                       class: "#{tab_box} #{is_active ? active_marker : 'border-transparent text-faint font-medium'}" do %>
            <%= tab[:label] %>
            <i class="bi bi-lock text-xs" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            <span class="sr-only"><%= reason %></span>
          <% end %>
          <% else %>
          <%= link_to tab[:path],
                "aria-current": (is_active ? active_tab_current : nil),
                class: "#{tab_box} transition-colors #{is_active ? active_marker : 'border-transparent text-cream-600 font-medium hover:text-cream-900 hover:border-cream-400'}" do %>
            <%= tab[:label] %>
          <% end %>
          <% end %>
        </li>
      <% end %>
    </ul>
  </nav>
<% end %>
